meta {
  name: ResolveFlow — the inheritance
  type: grpc
  seq: 2
}

grpc {
  url: {{coreGrpc}}
  method: /dop.v1.WorkflowService/ResolveFlow
  body: grpc
  auth: none
}

metadata {
  x-actor-id: {{actorId}}
  x-account-id: {{accountId}}
  x-request-id: {{$guid}}
}

body:grpc {
  [
    {
      "scope": "account",
      "scope_id": "{{accountId}}"
    }
  ]
}

docs {
  The domain's heart: the chain `platform ◁ account ◁ workspace ◁ project ◁ demand`
  resolved (ADR-0010). The most specific level wins, and the result says WHERE each
  stage came from.

  Notice `origins` and `contributors`: the provenance travels STRUCTURED, beyond
  the sentence in `resolved_from`. The sentence exists for a log and an error
  message; a contract that forces the consumer to interpret text breaks on the day
  somebody improves the wording.
}
